# npm always writes package.json and package-lock.json with LF. Seventeen
# door lockfiles were committed with CRLF, so the copy baked into the image
# never matched the copy npm regenerates on the volume when the entrypoint
# runs `npm install --omit=dev` - and the deploy's door-sync verification
# compares the two byte for byte. Every deploy therefore ended in a red X
# on a board that had deployed correctly.
*.json text eol=lf
package-lock.json text eol=lf
